Z"},"tree":{"sha":"b8b6b86ae0642862ed929318c856b2513dbe2cc3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cogni-dao/red/git/trees/b8b6b86ae0642862ed929318c856b2513dbe2cc3"},"message":"feat(cognition): bring node-template current with operator — mission + orientation (#48)\n\n* feat(cognition): node identity from repo-spec — intent.name + mission heading (sync-port hub #1701)\n\nPorts the node-identity surface from the operator hub (Cogni-DAO/cogni #1701)\nthat never reached node-template: forks inherited the cognition feature but not\nthe intent.mission heading, so every wizard-spawned node rendered the old\n'Cogni `<uuid>` — Session Cognition' header with no mission.\n\n- repo-spec schema: optional intent { name, mission } block\n- accessors: extractNodeName (intent.name → node_id fallback) + extractNodeMission\n- cognition contract: name + mission on the bundle response\n- shared/config: getNodeName / getNodeMission\n- cognition route + _bundle: render '<name> — Cogni Session Cognition' with a\n  mission · skills · domains · loaded subtitle (matches the hub bundle)\n- .cogni/repo-spec.yaml: a generic placeholder mission + forker guidance to\n  replace it (the node's one-line identity, surfaced at session start)\n- accessor unit coverage mirrored from the hub\n\nLoader (scripts/agent/session-cognition.sh) intentionally NOT touched —\nnode-template's two-account variant already self-resolves the node URL.\n\n* feat(cognition): orientation excerpt — port operator #1718 + #1735\n\nBrings node-template's cognition bundle fully current with operator main:\nthe bundle now surfaces a bounded (<=480 char) current-node orientation\nexcerpt from the <slug>-agent-orientation knowledge entry (node-specific\nwins over the inherited cogni-agent-orientation seed), with a 'seed one'\nfallback when absent. Also adopts #1735's tightened invariants/recall text\nand empty-domain suppression.\n\nFiles:\n- app/.../cognition/_bundle.ts: OrientationExcerpt + excerptFromContent +\n  render block + 